{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera","id":1037246,"title":"The Black Spiral and other Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-24T09:04:36-08:00","id":1037246,"title":"The Black Spiral and other Fera","content":"I'll make a long story short, as not to bother people with too many details: <br /> <br /> An acquiantance of mine does insist on playing a Fera who is also a Black Spiral Dancer. This ruffles my feathers well enough as it is - Black Spiral Dancers are pure NPCs as far as I'm concerned - but I am unsure as to how Fera other than the Garou can even dance the Black Spiral and survive. Especially since the second one requires the dancer to frenzy in order to complete it, so the Kitsune, for instance, would be unable to even finish it. <br /> <br /> I have gone through the W20 Book of the Wyrm and essentially found nothing explicitly for or against other Fera completing one or several circles, but I'm still sceptical at best - is there any hard, solid proof refuting or confirming my scepticism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:30:58-08:00","id":1037254,"title":"","content":"Fera don't become BSDs, they become other examples of tainted Fera, like Mnetics or Bitter Grins, hence the section for that in the W20 Book of the Wyrm..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:43:54-08:00","id":1037259,"title":"","content":"BSD are Garou. Their tribal gifts are balanced against the other Garou Gifts. <br /> <br /> You could be a tainted Fera that runs with a pack of BSDs I guess. You may even be able to dance the Spiral, though I am unsure which Fera would survive the encounter. But if you survived, you wouldn't be a BSD. You'll be something else. I don't know much about Fera, but I assume they have their own tribal structures with their own gifts. <br /> <br /> What Fera was your player thinking about playing? Is this a mixed game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:44:51-08:00","id":1037260,"title":"","content":"Apologies, I seem to have worded the question badly: It is not about whether other Fera can become BSDs (which is a Tribe, so naturally only Garou can join it), but whether they can Dance the Black Spiral altogether, regardless of further alliances. So its more like &quot;Can they learn the appropriate Rite&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:50:58-08:00","id":1037262,"title":"","content":"Probably, though their methods of corruption are different. They will probably go insane though, even if they are not corrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:19:28-08:00","id":1037273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1037262#post1037262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, though their methods of corruption are different. They will probably go insane though, even if they are not corrupted.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Corax could walk the Spiral and <i>not</i> be corrupted purely by dint of it being a bird rather than a wolf? What?<br /> <br /> Buzzards, Mnetics or Bale Sharks have different explanations about how they arise in their writeups, but that is not the only way that particular changing breed can be corrupted. If a Fera, any of them, treads the Black Spiral, they will belong to the Wyrm. You can't just dive headlong into the proverbial abyss without it changing you fundamentally for the worse. The will of the hardiest individual is nothing before the corrupt might of entropy made manifest.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: as a side note, OP, it sounds like you are only grudgingly allowing this player to be a Fera at all. It is your game- and some of the changing breeds are pretty powerful or highlight themes that may not be central to your story (I know I would struggle to incorporate, say, a Rokea, or a Nagah, in my own game).<br /> <br /> I would not reject the idea out of hand, but it sounds like your are being somehow forced into allowing this player to be whatever he wants... which might be the real issue here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 01-24-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:28:35-08:00","id":1037313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1037273#post1037273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a Corax could walk the Spiral and <i>not</i> be corrupted purely by dint of it being a bird rather than a wolf? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know better than that. The Corax have a different genesis (spirit egg vs. just being born) and a different charter purpose from Gaia. The Spiral Labyrinth could conceivably just snatch werewolves up due to their inborn purpose and leave others... well, not unaffected, but not wholly consumed, if consumed at all. It's paid forward by Corax having to reproduce by a taxing ritual that can be disrupted and turned back on itself to produce Buzzards. If a being gathered in tribes in the manner of Garou, it might be a different story, but they typically have more significant divisions than cultural ones, what with Bastet tribes being what kind of cat a character is and Mokole Streams being less distinct than tribes due to how Mnesis is more shared the further one goes back into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:11:28-08:00","id":1037348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1037313#post1037313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know better than that. The Corax have a different genesis (spirit egg vs. just being born) and a different charter purpose from Gaia. The Spiral Labyrinth could conceivably just snatch werewolves up due to their inborn purpose and leave others... well, not unaffected, but not wholly consumed, if consumed at all. It's paid forward by Corax having to reproduce by a taxing ritual that can be disrupted and turned back on itself to produce Buzzards. If a being gathered in tribes in the manner of Garou, it might be a different story, but they typically have more significant divisions than cultural ones, what with Bastet tribes being what kind of cat a character is and Mokole Streams being less distinct than tribes due to how Mnesis is more shared the further one goes back into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't accept that at all, and I find this perspective surprising. I think Garou were the only ones foolish enough to <i>enter</i> the Black Spiral Labyrinth, but I think if any other Fera had the gall to do so they would end up being just as unwholesome and evil afterward. I see nothing in the nature of the other changing breeds that describes the level of incorruptibility you seem to ascribe them.<br /> <br /> You are selling the Wyrm short if you think the only possible way it could spiritually corrupt a Corax is to do it while it is in the egg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:45:00-08:00","id":1037369,"title":"","content":"I think that their sanity would be blasted into pieces and, if vulnerable, would be subjected to many attempts for permanent possession, but I think that only Garou are corrupted in the fashion similar to the BSD. I think that the spiritual protections of their roles protect the other Fera from that specific threat, but they face other threats from the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:40:34-08:00","id":1037401,"title":"","content":"I am currently undecided on the Black Spiral Dancer Part. I have no trouble with said player playing a Fera, nor do I let them do as they please. I simply do not want to force my interpretation of the lore onto people without being able to back it up. Of course I can simply say &quot;This is what I'll go with, deal with it&quot;, but I prefer not doing so. Thank your all for the input so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:12:53-08:00","id":1037496,"title":"","content":"In revised the Ceilican had been ambushed by the BSD &amp; turned into Hellcats (i'm not sured if W20 changing breeds retconed that or slightly altered it, as in most Ceilican escaped that fate due to fae cat shenanigans)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:16:51-08:00","id":1037499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1037496#post1037496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In revised the Ceilican had been ambushed by the BSD &amp; turned into Hellcats (i'm not sured if W20 changing breeds retconed that or slightly altered it, as in most Ceilican escaped that fate due to fae cat shenanigans)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at that point, I could see how a developer might not want to devote all the word count that all of the particular corrupted versions of something might take. Especially the Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:21:28-08:00","id":1038040,"title":"","content":"Personally I think if a Fera gets tossed into the Spiral, they would end up as whatever the corrupted version of their type is. Sure there are other ways to get Balesharks or Bitter Grins, but dancing the Spiral should work just fine in addition to the more typical ways.<br /> <br /> I don't remember the exact tests for each layer of the Spiral, but I don't see why the other Fera couldn't work their way through offhand. I will have to go back and look it up when I get a chance later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:52:15-08:00","id":1038927,"title":"","content":"I'm of a mind that any Fera can decide to join the Wyrm, pledge themselves, be accepted, and become Wyrm tainted. And just use the rules for the BSD equivalent for their group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:13:24-08:00","id":1038963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1038927#post1038927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of a mind that any Fera can decide to join the Wyrm, pledge themselves, be accepted, and become Wyrm tainted. And just use the rules for the BSD equivalent for their group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. Though I think the thread specifically had the Spiral in mind and what effects it would have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:33:09-08:00","id":1038974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1038963#post1038963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this. Though I think the thread specifically had the Spiral in mind and what effects it would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Sorry, I might not have been specific enough. Were a Fera to dance the spiral, I think it would have a comparable effect as to turn them into their relative Wyrm-Fera versions. Something I would think would occur in any extreme cause of Wyrm taint/joining the Wyrm. Not that I particularly have anything in the books to back that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:25:35-08:00","id":1039000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1038974#post1038974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure. Sorry, I might not have been specific enough. Were a Fera to dance the spiral, I think it would have a comparable effect as to turn them into their relative Wyrm-Fera versions. Something I would think would occur in any extreme cause of Wyrm taint/joining the Wyrm. Not that I particularly have anything in the books to back that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fault for misunderstanding.<br /> So yea, this is my take on it too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:36:26-08:00","id":1039012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1039000#post1039000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My fault for misunderstanding.<br /> So yea, this is my take on it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, entire on me. I think it seemed a little unclear as far as the question. Is becoming a Fera Black Spiral Dancer meant to be the equivalent of said Tainted Fera or just a Fera with access to BSD gifts? Not sure on the details there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:48:14-08:00","id":1039022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1039012#post1039012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, no, entire on me. I think it seemed a little unclear as far as the question. Is becoming a Fera Black Spiral Dancer meant to be the equivalent of said Tainted Fera or just a Fera with access to BSD gifts? Not sure on the details there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, just speaking from my point of view: the Fera isn't becoming a Spiral (as in Garou Tribe) so they shouldn't get access to BSD Gifts. I suppose you could call them Black Spiral Dancers if they physically/spiritually dance the Spiral (since the term would be literally correct), but I think that gets a bit confusing.<br /> <br /> I would just have them go on to be whatever the tainted version of their Fera is and call them as such. To me, the means by which they become tainted is less important than the end result.<br /> <br /> So a Rokea thrown into the Spiral would come out (assuming they survive) as a Bale Shark for all intents and purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:29:38-08:00","id":1040082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1039022#post1039022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Rokea thrown into the Spiral would come out (assuming they survive) as a Bale Shark for all intents and purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balefire Sharks are created through a pact with Lord Kerne, the Maeljin Incarna of Balefire; I suppose a Rokea going through the Black Spiral would be different from them - not having radiation-related capabilities and not having to listen to Lord Kerne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-29-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:22:00-08:00","id":1040103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1040082#post1040082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Sharks are created through a pact with Lord Kerne, the Maeljin Incarna of Balefire; I suppose a Rokea going through the Black Spiral would be different from them - not having radiation-related capabilities and not having to listen to Lord Kerne.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see little reason the same thing can't happen in the Spiral.<br /> Admittedly, I hadn't gone back and read the section in W20 until just now. Having read it again, there could be a difference, but I stand by the idea that the resulting Spiral-Shark could still be close enough that the differences are negligible for most story's purposes. The section for Balefire Sharks even says they can learn BSD Gifts, so really all you are trading out (if you go that route) is the Balefire healing and radioactive dependency. As per listening to Lord Kerne, they will likely just end up with a different Maeljin (or other Wyrm Incarna) barking orders at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:38:32-08:00","id":1040149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1037246-the-black-spiral-and-other-fera?p=1040103#post1040103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see little reason the same thing can't happen in the Spiral.<br /> Admittedly, I hadn't gone back and read the section in W20 until just now. Having read it again, there could be a difference, but I stand by the idea that the resulting Spiral-Shark could still be close enough that the differences are negligible for most story's purposes. The section for Balefire Sharks even says they can learn BSD Gifts, so really all you are trading out (if you go that route) is the Balefire healing and radioactive dependency. As per listening to Lord Kerne, they will likely just end up with a different Maeljin (or other Wyrm Incarna) barking orders at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call that they could very well make the pact with Lord Kerne in (or perhaps after) the Black Spiral. And yes the difference is negligible in most stories - unless you are playing a Wyrmish Rokea game, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T03:50:45-08:00","id":1042877,"title":"","content":"I think, as this is the Umbra, the path might be 'the Spiral', but it won't be the Spiral as the BSD tribe knows it. The path to corruption isn't the same for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}